From 1f19ecd1af965b5ccfddc0ff46266b68eaa9ed12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bowen Wang <wangbowen1001@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 15:11:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(pcg): clean Y for VLM deepstack via warmup context
 manager

R4.C lesson: a multimodal warmup pass cannot bypass
set_attention_metadata_context() (which the regular _run_dummy_forward
sets up via _run_forward); calling self.model(...) directly inside a
torch.compile-traced region trips an in-trace data-dependent
assertion at forward_context.py:59 and Dynamo aborts the compile
under fullgraph=True. This patch implements the clean Y design from
plan.md so the multimodal Dynamo branch is compiled at warmup with
the forward context properly set up.

Design:

mm_utils.py:
  - Module-local thread-local `_force_warmup_deepstack_tls` and a
    `force_warmup_deepstack_embeds()` contextmanager that flips it
    on inside `with`-blocks and restores the prior value.
  - `general_mm_embed_routine` gains a new branch BETWEEN the
    existing `contains_mm_inputs()` real-mm path and the text-only
    `else`: when the gate is active AND `use_deepstack` is truthy
    AND the multimodal_model exposes `config.hidden_size` and
    `num_deepstack_embeddings`, the routine embed-tokens the
    input_ids and synthesizes
    `kwargs["input_deepstack_embeds"] = torch.zeros(
        [num_tokens, hidden_size * num_deepstack_embeddings],
        dtype, device)`.
    The routine then calls `language_model(...)` exactly as before,
    so the forward context plumbing (already established by the
    surrounding _run_forward in the warmup driver) stays intact.

tc_piecewise_cuda_graph_backend.py:
  - Imports `force_warmup_deepstack_embeds` from mm_utils.
  - Adds `_model_has_deepstack()` predicate that inspects the
    language model's `use_deepstack` attribute. Models without that
    attribute (or with all values falsy) pay zero cost.
  - In `_run_compile_pass`, after the existing text-only
    `Compile-num-tokens` loop, opens
    `with force_warmup_deepstack_embeds():` and runs a second
    per-shape `Compile MM num tokens` loop that calls the EXISTING
    `cuda_graph_runner._run_dummy_forward(num_tokens)` -- so
    `_run_forward` wraps the call with
    `set_attention_metadata_context()` as it always has, and the
    Dynamo compile inside fullgraph=True does NOT hit the
    forward_context assert.

Effect:
  - During warmup, Dynamo traces BOTH branches of
    `Qwen3LLMModel.forward` (input_deepstack_embeds=None and
    input_deepstack_embeds=non-None). The piecewise CUDA graph
    backend then captures cuda graphs for both Dynamo frames during
    the subsequent capture_session.
  - At inference, the first real image request hits a captured graph
    rather than forcing a runtime recompile. No missing-capture-
    stream fallback. No (X)-style eager regression.
  - Text-only models and other VLMs without deepstack go through
    the unmodified code path; no observable change.

To be validated on the E2a recipe (image 720p, c=1, n=32, warmup=30,
PCG on, IPC on, GPU 0) then stretched to n=400. Performance gate per
plan.md: TTFT p50 must clearly beat the PCG-off baseline of 64.8 ms.
